  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "One candle is 20 cm long and takes 3 hours to burn completely. A second candle is 25 cm long and takes 2 hours to burn completely. If both candles are lit at the same time, then find the time taken for the second candle to be exactly half the height of the first candle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{18}{11}$ hours.",
      "worked": "The burn rates are $\\dfrac{20}{3}$ cm/hour and $\\dfrac{25}{2}$ cm/hour. After $t$ hours, the heights are $20-\\dfrac{20}{3}t$ cm and $25-\\dfrac{25}{2}t$ cm.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}25-\\frac{25}{2}t&=\\frac12\\left(20-\\frac{20}{3}t\\right)\\\\150-75t&=60-20t\\\\150&=60+55t\\\\90&=55t\\\\t&=\\frac{18}{11}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe second candle is half the height of the first after $\\dfrac{18}{11}$ hours.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
